the u.s surgeon general is calling covid  vaccine  misinformation an imminent and insidious  threat  that very stark warning was prompted by  a nationwide surge in cases of this  highly contagious  delta variant in a public advisory dr  vivek murthy says  false information shared on social media  is a serious threat to public health  that is driving vaccine hesitancy he  wrote that misinformation is fueling  fears  about possible side effects and led to  people to declare people to decline  covet 19 vaccines  nearly 56 percent of americans have  received at least  one vaccine dose u.s surgeon general dr  vivek morthy joins us now good morning  thanks for being with us good morning  what action do you want to see taken to  effectively stop this misinformation  well yesterday i issued a surgeon  general's advisory on health  misinformation  because i'm deeply concerned about the  impact this is happening on our health  and to be clear about what this is  health misinformation  is information that's false inaccurate  or misleading  about our health according to the best  evidence at the time  and as a doctor i've seen the impact  that this has had on patients i've seen  people struggle  to make medical decisions for themselves  and their families because they  they can't make sense of the conflicting  and often false stories you're seeing on  social media  but the good news is that there is  something we can do about this but it's  going to take all of us  working together individuals for example  can check their sources  before they share stories online is it  coming from a scientifically credible  source  and if you're not sure don't share but  we really need our tech companies to  step up here as well  because we know that so much of this  information is being transacted on  technology platforms  dr murthy in in our reporting earlier in  this broadcast  it came out that that this is actually  sourced back to a relatively few  uh initial sources do you have any sense  of why this misinformation is being  spread  well it's an interesting question and  there are several reasons but two that  i'll point out to in some cases there  are people  intentionally trying to spread  information sometimes for financial gain  or for political reasons or for other  reasons but we also know that  much of the misinformation out there is  often spread by people  who actually don't have bad intentions  there are people like me and you and  others who are listening today who might  see a story that they think is alarming  and they think  sharing it with their network might be  helpful to them they may not realize  it's false  and that's why in this advisory we we  physically point  to the steps that individuals can take  to pause before they share but it's also  why technology companies have  a really important role here to plan  identifying super spreaders of  misinformation  in stopping uh their activity and spread  the misinformation online  and it also helped in being more  transparent so we understand  just how much misinformation is being  transacted on these platforms and what  strategies are working to stop it  part of the reason why i think dr murphy  is so confusing let's start with los  angeles where now  even if you're vaccinated you have to  wear a mask  it just seems like the rules keep  changing because we're always told if  you're vaccinated  you're safe i call it my superpower it  protects you so why do  vaccinated people also now have to wear  a mask in los  angeles if supposedly you're safe with  the vaccine  so gail you're pointing to a really  important issue here this is we've seen  this as a challenge throughout this  pandemic  which is that as science evolves our  guidance has to also evolve  but if we're not able to communicate  that with enough context and clarity and  consistency then it can lead to  confusion  and right now with masks for example one  of the things we know is the science  tells us that if you are fully  vaccinated that's two weeks after your  last shot  your chances of getting sick and  transmitting the infection to somebody  else are low  that doesn't mean zero it means a low so  there are certain circumstances where if  you have  a lot of virus in your community around  you or if you are somebody who lives at  home with people who are unvaccinated  that you might choose  to continue wearing masks and localities  like la county or other  counties that are looking around and  seeing cases rising and seeing large  portions of people unvaccinated may  choose  to put measures back in place like mass  requirements  and that flexibility is okay but what  we've got to do is  consistently clearly and transparently  communicate with people about  what these rules are why they may be  shifting because otherwise it can be  very confusing  yeah i was very sorry to hear doctor  that you lost 10 members of your own  family to this  this to covet i'm sure you tried to  convince them to get the vaccine  so what do you say to people that just  don't get it  well gail first of all thank you and my  family members who  you know who have passed away  unfortunately due to covet  they didn't have a chance actually to  get fully vaccinated the vast majority  of them and i  think so often about things could have  been different if they did have a  vaccine available to them but for those  out there who are still  unsure of whether they should get  vaccinated number one i try  to listen uh to their concerns that's  something i was taught earlier in  medicine you don't judge people for  their beliefs you  you listen to them you try to understand  and then i also try to make sure that  they have access  to the information that science actually  guides us to understand about his  vaccine not the myths that are out there  in the midst of two-thirds of  unvaccinated people unfortunately  either believe or think or true but the  real facts and the facts are this  that these vaccines are our single most  powerful pathway to ending this pandemic  they've saved  thousands of lives already the benefits  of vaccinations certainly far outweigh  any rare risks that come with them so  as a doctor i urge people to look at the  data make the best decision for yourself  and your family  but know that they're saving lives right  now yeah i hear you and we will keep  repeating that information as often as  we need to thank you so much for joining  us this morning  thank you
 

