 vaccinated that's two weeks after your  last shot  your chances of getting sick and  transmitting the infection to somebody  else are low  that doesn't mean zero it means a low so  there are certain circumstances where if  you have  a lot of virus in your community around  you or if you are somebody who lives at  home with people who are unvaccinated  that you might choose  to continue wearing masks and localities  like la county or other  counties that are looking around and  seeing cases rising and seeing large  portions of people unvaccinated may  choose  to put measures back in place like mass  requirements  and that flexibility is okay but what  we've got to do is  consistently clearly and transparently  communicate with people about  what these rules are why they may be  shifting because otherwise it can be  very confusing  yeah i was very sorry to hear doctor  that you lost 10 members of your own  family to this  this to covet i'm sure you tried to  convince them to get the vaccine  so what do you say to people that just  don't get it  well gail first of all thank you and my  family members who  you know who have passed away  unfortunately due to covet  they didn't have a chance actually to  get fully vaccinated the vast majority  of them and i  think so often about things could have  been different if they did have a  vaccine available to them but for those  out there who are still  unsure of whether they should get  vaccinated number one i try  to listen uh to their concerns that's  something i was taught earlier in  medicine you don't judge people for  their beliefs you  you listen to them you try to understand  and then i also try to make sure that  they have access  to the information that science actually  guides us to understand about his  vaccine not the myths that are out there  in the midst of two-thirds of  unvaccinated people unfortunately  either believe or think or true but the  real facts and the facts are this  that these vaccines are our single most  powerful pathway to ending this pandemic  they've saved  thousands of lives already the benefits  of vaccinations certainly far outweigh  any rare risks that come with them so  as a doctor i urge people to look at the  data make the best decision for yourself  and your family  but know that they're saving lives right  now yeah i hear you and we will keep  repeating that information as often as  we need to thank you so much for joining  us this morning  thank you


